hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21472","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us from al-Zuhri from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham from Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed of poetry is wisdom."
"21473","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu Kamil narrated to us, both saying: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us from al-Zuhri, Abu Kamil saying in his hadith: Ibn Shihab narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Abdullah ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed of poetry is wisdom. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Thus Ibrahim ibn Sad says in his hadith: Abdullah ibn al-Aswad, and it is rather Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth from Ubayy ibn Kab, thus says other than Ibrahim ibn Sad."
"21474","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Abu Bakr from Marwan from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed of poetry is wisdom."
"21475","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar informed us from al-Zuhri from Urwah from Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith. My father said: And Ibn al-Mubarak agreed with him, meaning they agreed upon Urwah, and did not say Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"21476","Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abdullah informed us: Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Abdullah ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed of poetry is wisdom."
"21477","Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak said: And Mamar narrated to me similar to it exactly, save he put in place of Abu Bakr Urwah."
"21478","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us: Rabah narrated to us from Mamar from al-Zuhri: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me from Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from Ubayy ibn Kab that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed of poetry is wisdom. And Rabah contradicted the narration of Ibn al-Mubarak and Abd al-Razzaq, for they both said: From Urwah. Rabah said: From Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"21479","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Mukram and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to me, both saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Yunus from al-Zuhri: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me from Marwan from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from Ubayy from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Yunus informed us from al-Zuhri: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"21480","Rawh narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Ziyad, meaning Ibn Sad, informed me that Ibn Shihab informed him, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me from Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad that Ubayy informed him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"21481","Abdullah narrated to us: Amr al-Naqid narrated to me: al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani al-Rusafi narrated to us: my grandfather Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us from al-Zuhri: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed him from Marwan ibn al-Hakam that Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth informed him from Ubayy ibn Kab, he informed him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"21482","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to me: al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us from al-Zuhri, saying: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, saying: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth say: I heard Ubayy ibn Kab say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and he mentioned it, and he did not mention Marwan in it."
"21483","Abdullah narrated to us, saying: And Abu Mamar narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us from Ibn Shihab from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Marwan ibn al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Abd Yaghuth from Ubayy ibn Kab from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Thus Abu Mamar narrated it to us from Ibrahim ibn Sad, and said therein Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, and Abu Mamar contradicted the narration of those who narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Sad, for a number narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Sad and said therein: From Abdullah ibn al-Aswad."
